    "title": "Emmy Noether: Modern LaTeX Working Corpus and Multilingual Translation Drafts (Integrated v26 Source-Control Update)",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21312393",
    "publication_date": "2026-07-11",
    "description": "<p>This is the reader-facing Emmy Noether working record for the Modern LaTeX Editions of Mathematics Manuscripts project. This version fronts <code>00_Noether_German_Cumulative_Working_SourceControl_v26_20260711.pdf</code>, a 466-page German source-control reader, and supplies the integrated v26 TeX, source witnesses, page dispositions, correction ledgers, diffs, render checks, prior-chain evidence, and build logs in <code>07_Noether_Current_German_SourceControl_v26_20260711.zip</code>.</p><p><strong>What changed:</strong> the v20-v26 chain extends direct source comparison beyond the previous v19 release. It records Paper 34 through printed p. 692, current-head page passes for Papers 35-39, a Paper 41 regression repair, five integrated R817 Paper 19 corrections, and a page-disposition ledger for all 21 printed pages of Paper 43. The newest v26 repair restores seven atomic Paper 43 loci, including two occurrences of <code>alpha = alpha e</code>, a congruence modulo <code>S_i</code>, and the heading <em>Komponentenzerlegung der Differente</em>. The grouped ZIP has one safe root and a verified 882-row SHA-256 manifest.</p><p><strong>Status caveat:</strong> this is a serious source-repair and translation working corpus, not OCR-only, but it is not a critical edition, author-wide source-faithfulness certification, paper-by-paper certification, multilingual synchronization, or publication-grade proofreading. The retained English and multilingual readers predate some German repairs. Inherited words such as <code>COMPLETE</code>, <code>closure</code>, or <code>closed</code> refer only to bounded local audit tasks. A newer R818 Paper 20 packet and an active v27 Paper 40 directory remain unintegrated continuation inputs and are not competing public heads.</p><p><strong>GitHub:</strong> corrections, source comparisons, LaTeX fixes, and translation improvements can be suggested via issues or pull requests at <a href=\"https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts\">https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts</a>.</p>",
